 "explanation": "Requires the NRPN reception patch (shared anti-echo flag [address]). [routine] (every knob edit of a sound parameter) calls [routine] only when the value changed; that call now goes to a hook (0x9d07a400) that first makes the original call, then, if the change did not come from MIDI ([address] = 0) and Remote Pad OUT is not Off, sends NRPN p with the new value on channel Remote Pad OUT - 1: CC 99 = p >> 7, CC 98 = p & 0x7f, CC 6 = value >> 7, CC 38 = value & 0x7f, each as a full-status message on DIN ([routine], [routine], until now unused) and on USB ([routine], [routine]), like note-on [routine]. Same whitelist as the reception: 0-126 and 156/157 (Osc 3/4 sample, 0-463, read as 128 * byte[15/21] + byte[14/20]). Not echoed: the Frequency changed by a Fine overflow ([routine] writes it directly), sound loads, beat-wide offsets ([routine]), Revert. The DIN send ring (0x800 bytes) has no overflow check: each echo is 12 bytes (3.8 ms of DIN time). Code added at 0x9d07a400-0x9d07a53b (79 words).",
